KNOWNBUG
main.py
--no-signed-overflow-check
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
Python integers don't overflow, but CBMC generates signed overflow
checks for all arithmetic. With 64-bit ints, small constants don't
trigger this, but nondet values or large expressions do.
Fix: pass --no-signed-overflow-check by default for Python, or use
unsigned types. Affects ~10 ESBMC tests.
